{
  "id": "06065_kitaisuru",
  "headword": "{期待|きたい}する",
  "reading": "きたいする",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (suru)",
  "gloss": "to expect, to hope for",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to expect, to hope for, to look forward to",
      "explanation": "To anticipate something positive happening or to have hopes for a good outcome."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06065_kitaisuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{良|よ}い{結果|けっか}を{期待|きたい}している。",
      "english": "I'm hoping for good results.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06065_kitaisuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "あまり{期待|きたい}しないでください。",
      "english": "Please don't expect too much.",
      "notes": "Lowering expectations",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06065_kitaisuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{君|きみ}には{期待|きたい}しているよ。",
      "english": "I have high hopes for you.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06065_kitaisuru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{期待|きたい}に{応|こた}えられるように{頑張|がんば}ります。",
      "english": "I'll do my best to meet your expectations.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06065_kitaisuru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{新|あたら}しい{映画|えいが}に{期待|きたい}していたが、{期待|きたい}はずれだった。",
      "english": "I was looking forward to the new movie, but it was a letdown.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: Xに{期待|きたい}する (expect from X / have hopes for X) / Xを{期待|きたい}する (expect/hope for X).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates ongoing state. {期待|きたい}している = 'is expecting' or 'has expectations.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{期待|きたい}に{応|こた}える (meet expectations)\n・{期待|きたい}を{裏切|うらぎ}る (betray expectations)\n・{期待|きたい}はずれ (disappointment; let-down)\n・{期待|きたい}が{高|たか}まる (expectations rise)\n\nNUANCE: Implies a positive, hopeful anticipation. Different from {予想|よそう}する which is more neutral.",
